# Git — conventions

- Commit message — in **English**, subject in the log style: `- <plan|what>: <why>` (see `git log` — one line, no extra sections).
- **Agree on the commit text with the user before `git commit`** — propose a subject, wait for ok.
- No attribution trailers (`Generated with`, `Co-Authored-By`, etc.) — authorship comes from git config.
- Separate commits per plan: P-changes to prod code and to test hygiene are not mixed in one commit. Exception — remediation (a review-fix plan) editing the same files the parent feature introduces in the same uncommitted package: fold into the feature commit (don't fabricate an intermediate state that never compiled); plan docs remain separate.
- Don't push without an explicit request; don't edit git config.
